{{smaller block|''Vulpicide'', committed in defence of property, and condemned neither by religion, nor by equity, nor by any law save that of sportsmen, excites an anger that cries aloud for positive penalties.
{{right|''H. Spencer'', Study of Sociol., p. 245.}}}}

