'''vulpinism''' (vul′pi-nizm), ''n.'' [< ''vulpine'' + ''-ism.''] The property of being vulpine; craft; artfulness; cunning. ''Carlyle.''

'''vulpinite''' (vul′pi-nīt), ''n.'' [< ''Vulpino'' (see def.) + ''-ite''<sup>2</sup>.] A scaly granular variety of the mineral anhydrite. {{smaller|It occurs at Vulpino in Italy, and is sometimes employed for small statues and other ornamental work under the name of ''marino bardiglio.''}}

