'''Vultur''' (vul′tėr), ''n.'' [NL.: see ''vulture''.] A Linnean genus of ''Falconidæ'', variously defined. {{smaller|(''a''†) Including all the vultures of both hemispheres. (''b'') Restricted to certain Old World vultures, as ''V. monachus''.}}

